  "light_side": {
    "value": "right",
    "why": "Living-room evening: the window is dusk-dark; lamps are on at both sides. The tall floor lamp on the right is the brightest region of room_evening and sits at head/shoulder height. The left table lamp is lower and smaller. x=295 is left of that floor lamp (and left of the table), so the character's lit side is still the right. World direction; a flip would keep the world-right side."
  },
  "stray_left_hand": {
    "cause": "Open gap wider than 1 px between the left (back-lit) arm and the torso at sprite (16,87) and (17,87), just under the left fingertips. The hole flood and 1-px-channel rules missed it (the gap is open to the outside and at y=87 is two pixels wide). Those transparent pixels had the arm directly to their left, so the right-facing (light-side) neighbour test treated them as a lit edge. They are well below the top cutoff, so they were not isTop.",
    "fix": "A light-side rim pixel is kept only if a same-row scan TOWARD the light (to the canvas edge on the light side; world direction, localLight already includes flip) meets no opaque sprite pixel — only the outermost light-side contour. Scanning toward the back-lit side would KEEP the stray dots (and also (17,43)/(18,43)), so that phrasing is the wrong direction. The same unoccluded idea is applied to the top rim: nothing opaque above in the same column, so an upward-facing edge inside a notch is not lit.",
    "removed_sprite_xy": [
      [
        16,
        87
      ],
      [
        17,
        87
      ]
    ],
    "present_in_new_shots": false
  }
